---
title: Estimate versions — a revision always needs fresh approval
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Draft (editable)" as draft
  state "Sent — waiting for customer" as sent
  state "Approved" as approved
  state "Partly approved" as partial
  state "Declined" as rejected
  state "Withdrawn" as withdrawn
  state "Superseded" as superseded

  [*] --> draft: Start estimate (version 1)
  draft --> sent: Send — version is frozen, link issued
  sent --> approved: Customer approves every line
  sent --> partial: Customer approves some lines
  sent --> rejected: Customer declines everything
  sent --> withdrawn: Revision started before the customer decided — link dies
  approved --> superseded: Newer version sent — link dies
  partial --> superseded: Newer version sent
  rejected --> superseded: Newer version sent
  withdrawn --> [*]
  superseded --> [*]

  note right of draft
    A revision is a new version (N + 1).
    It copies the latest lines with every
    line back to "pending". Approvals from
    earlier versions never carry over.
  end note
  note left of sent
    Prices, lines and terms can't change
    once sent — the database refuses it.
    One link per version; a new link
    replaces the old one.
  end note
